{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 557 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D16"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the bacteriostatic water shortage on 2021-12-03 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E38"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our product label names Hospira, Inc. as labeler and lists three registered plants: Hospira, Inc. FEI 1021343, Hospira, Inc. FEI 1925262, and Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited FEI 3008316085.",
      "cites": ["E15", "E27", "E36"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited (FEI 3008316085) received an OAI classification letter dated 2020-05-25, 557 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1925262) received an OAI classification letter dated 2020-04-22, 590 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343) received a Warning Letter on 2010-04-12 and multiple OAI inspections in 2010 and 2011.",
      "cites": ["E14", "E5", "E7", "E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑based best option is to buy from Fujian Genohope Biotech Ltd., which is not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D19"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A secondary option is a protocol change to Sterile Water 1 mL/mL from Nephron Pharmaceuticals Corporation, approved 2026-07-09.",
      "cites": ["D20"]
    }
  ]
}
